Hi Gurpreet,

Here is a short update on where we are with ENTS automation, for you and the ENTS team.

New this sprint

Transfer approval in ENTS Core. We have added [number] test cases that approve a submitted transfer in ENTS Core. Until now our journeys stopped once the transferee accepted and the transfer was submitted. They now carry on through approval, so each transfer is checked end to end: created, accepted, submitted and approved.

Where the ENTS pack stands

Coverage. 25 end-to-end test cases run on the Playwright framework. They cover agent, individual and ETF partner transfers across every transfer type, plus appeals and the NR/CISYF applications.
Latest full run. 21 of the 25 passed, and the whole pack finished in 1 hour 26 minutes. The run submitted 75 transfers.
Speed. The previous regression suite took over 10 hours for ENTS, so results are now ready the same morning.
Nightly runs. The pack runs every night on Jenkins without anyone starting it, and each run publishes a dashboard with the result of every test case.

Stability work completed

Test data. Herds and logins are taken from the database before each run, so the weekly CENTEST refresh no longer breaks the tests.
Herds with no entitlements. When an individual transferor turns out to have none, the test now picks another herd and carries on instead of failing.
ETF partner acceptance. The test now waits for the page to settle before searching, which removed an intermittent failure.
Document upload. Individual logins see a different list of document types, and the test now handles both.

What we are working on next

Fixing the 4 test cases that failed in the latest run. Two are down to ETF partner test data and two are timing issues on a screen.
Extending the ENTS Core coverage beyond approval.
Starting the framework training for the ENTS and BISS testers, so the team can run the pack and triage results themselves.

